// M3 field-report corpus (PLAN-D10/MECH-D13, wave 3, finding 2): the lever's basic toggle,
// oracle-verified. Every block_id/state_id below was resolved directly against the generated
// registry (`crates/registries/generated/v776/block_state_properties.rs`'s `STATE_PROPERTIES`/
// `BLOCK_RANGES` arrays for `minecraft:lever` = `block_id` 520, range `[6771, 6794]`, default
// `6780` = face=wall/facing=north/powered=false; `block_states.rs`'s own `STONE` default-state
// constant).
//
// Deliberately does NOT chain a redstone-wire reader (fetch-corpus's own self-validating
// state-id pairing surfaced a real, separately-reported cross-cutting gap when an earlier draft
// of this fixture put a wire directly adjacent to the lever: a `ctx.set_block`-driven toggle
// (the lever's own MECH-D82 flag-3 write) reaching an adjacent wire tile within the same settle
// pass processes that wire's own `on_neighbor_changed` (power) and `on_shape_update`
// (connections) in an order that can silently revert the just-applied power digit while also
// recomputing a different connection shape than the real oracle -- `docs/findings-for-planning
// .md`'s own entry has the full citation and reproduction. That gap is a general redstone-
// dispatch-ordering question, not specific to the lever (every tier-1 signal source that ever
// toggles beside a wire via a flag-3-equivalent write could trigger it) -- this fixture's own
// scope stays the lever's own state transition, which `redstone_lever.rs`'s and
// `play_lever_field_report.rs`'s own direct assertions (the latter over a real production
// server connection) already independently confirm weak-signal propagation for.
ContraptionSpec(
    id: "redstone/qc/lever_powers_wire_via_state_swap",
    category: QcShowcase,
    description: "A wall-mounted lever (facing east, mounted on a stone to its west), toggled via a direct powered-state swap, then toggled back off.",
    quirk: "LeverBlock.useWithoutItem cycles POWERED via level.setBlock(pos, state, 3) -- the lever's own raw block-state id is the only observable this fixture asserts.",
    max_ticks: 6,
    blocks: [
        (pos: (0, 0, 0), vanilla_state: "minecraft:stone", state_id: 1),
        (pos: (1, 0, 0), vanilla_state: "minecraft:lever[face=wall,facing=east,powered=false]", state_id: 6786),
    ],
    actions: [
        // Tick 3: flip the lever in place from powered=false to powered=true (this project's
        // own state-id-swap action convention, standing in for a real player pull() -- there is
        // no in-game interact/use packet path this replay harness drives directly).
        (tick: 3, pos: (1, 0, 0), vanilla_state: "minecraft:lever[face=wall,facing=east,powered=true]", state_id: 6785),
        // Tick 5: flip it back off.
        (tick: 5, pos: (1, 0, 0), vanilla_state: "minecraft:lever[face=wall,facing=east,powered=false]", state_id: 6786),
    ],
)
